    "result_text": "The full suite (the single `AcceptanceTest`, plus `AcceptanceBase`) passes and the build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `sharesHousehold` \u2192 shared `householdId` behavior on `POST /api/owners`, keeping each piece of logic in its own small unit.\n\n**What each owner sharing a household gets:** when a create-owner request sets `sharesHousehold: true`, the new owner and every existing owner in the same household (same last name + address, normalized) are all assigned the same stable `householdId`, and that id is returned on the owner.\n\nChanges:\n\n- **`OwnerHouseholds`** (shared household identity) \u2014 added `id(lastName, address)`, which derives a stable, shared `HH-<12 hex>` identifier from the existing canonical household `key(...)`. Deterministic from the key, so every owner in the same household resolves to the same value regardless of creation order. Reuses the existing normalization rather than duplicating it.\n- **`AssignOwnerHousehold`** (new function, single responsibility) \u2014 a no-op unless `sharesHousehold` is true; otherwise sets the derived `householdId` on the new owner and backfills the same id onto existing household members. It complements, rather than merges into, `RequireUniqueHousehold` (which owns the reject-vs-allow decision).\n- **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired `assignHousehold` into the pipeline right after `build` (so the built `Owner` entity exists), under `govern: [ transaction ]`.\n- **`Owner` entity** \u2014 added the persisted `household_id` column with getter/setter.\n- **DB schemas** (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) \u2014 added the `household_id` column.\n- **openapi.yml** \u2014 added the read-only `householdId` property to the `Owner` response schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gets the field and MapStruct maps it automatically (so both the create response and `GET /api/owners/{id}` return it). `sharesHousehold` stays a write-only, non-stored request directive.\n\nThe design keeps DTOs at the edges, derives the shared id from the one existing household key definition, and adds no unrelated logic to any existing class.",
